    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0345" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg325"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pike to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 151.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 10, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: * * * * * *</p>
                <p>There has never been a time since the war began when the current of public
                    opinion in Europe was setting so irresistibly towards the conclusion that the
                    rebellion must succumb as it is doing now.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES S. PIKE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
